 "detector": {
  "what": "ONE detector, adopted from scripts/audit_results_binder_forms.py: its find_rows() is loaded BY PATH by scripts/list_results_binders.py, which then classifies every row BY ITS DESTINATION -- never by syntax. A writer is bound by where it writes.",
  "classes": {
   "record_binder": "<worktree>/results, or an absolute literal into the legacy record or one of its declared duplicate copies. TARGET 0.",
   "named_write_destination": "a named directory's own results/ (darts/results). TARGET 0.",
   "log_coordinate": "DECLARED, and NOT residue: deferred:log-coordinate:t_c442023d with landed_by 8f51ae8 -- t_c442023d re-pointed them at cabinet_root.log_dir()/log_path() and LOG_EDGES.json carries them."
  },
  "why": "the counter's two os.path.join patterns could not see depth_test.py:27 (an absolute literal) or darts/darts.py:706 (os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), 'results')). The blindness was one layer out from the pattern, and it is now the detector's job."
 },
